    "show_share": true,
    "description": "AKU has been at the forefront of the provincial, national and international response to an outbreak of HIV/AIDS that infected nearly 1,200 children in Larkana District, Sindh. The University was the first to alert officials of an outbreak, and has been advising government, providing patient care and training health workers, as well as publishing the most in-depth study of the outbreak to date, in The Lancet Infectious Diseases.",
